{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2152-07-27 23:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee, one of the hospitalists. I’ll be taking care of you tonight. Can you tell me what brought you in?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2152-07-27 23:52:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, yes. I had that MRCP with secretin yesterday, and shortly after, I started having that same sharp pain in my upper belly—epigastric, like before. It’s been getting worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2152-07-27 23:54:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, and any nausea? Vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2152-07-27 23:55:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, nausea for sure, but I haven’t thrown up. I’ve had this before after the MRCP—last time it flared up too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2152-07-27 23:57:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. Given your history of chronic pancreatitis, the secretin can sometimes trigger a flare. We’ve checked your blood work, and your lipase is elevated—662—so this does look like another episode of acute pancreatitis on top of your chronic condition."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2152-07-27 23:59:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, great. So it’s not just me imagining it. What happens now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2152-07-28 00:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep you NPO—for now, no food or drink by mouth—to let your pancreas rest. We’ll give you IV fluids to stay hydrated and Dilaudid for pain control. You’ll also get medication for nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2152-07-28 00:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I remember Zofran usually helps, but I’m allergic to that, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2152-07-28 00:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’re allergic to Zofran. We’ve given you Phenergan initially and will switch to Reglan, which should help with nausea without the risk."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2152-07-28 00:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. And my anxiety’s been worse with the pain. I take clonazepam and fluoxetine—can I keep those?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2152-07-28 00:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve continued your fluoxetine, imipramine, and clonazepam. We’ll also have Ativan available if you need extra help with nausea or anxiety."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2152-07-28 00:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I just want to get through this flare."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2152-07-28 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling? Pain level?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2152-07-28 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still some pain, maybe a 5 out of 10. Nausea’s a bit better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2152-07-28 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your lipase this morning dropped to 100, which is a good sign—your pancreas is calming down. We’ll keep you on IV fluids and pain meds for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2152-07-28 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. What about the MRCP results? Did they show anything new?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2152-07-28 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the scan showed more dilation of the pancreatic duct after secretin, and it didn’t return to normal after 10 minutes. There’s also irregularity in the duct and more side branches—signs of chronic pancreatitis. It also suggests possible sphincter of Oddi dysfunction."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2152-07-28 08:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So that’s why I keep flaring after the test? Is there a fix?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2152-07-28 08:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s likely a contributing factor. GI has been consulted. They recommend treating the acute flare now and planning an outpatient EUS—endoscopic ultrasound—to get a better look. They’ll contact you to schedule it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2152-07-28 08:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds like a plan. I just hope we can figure this out."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2152-07-29 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We’re going to try advancing your diet today—start with clear liquids. How’s the pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2152-07-29 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better, maybe a 3 now. I’m nervous about eating—last time it made it worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2152-07-29 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Totally understandable. We’ll go slow—clear liquids first, and if you tolerate it, we’ll move to soft foods tomorrow. We’ll monitor closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2152-07-29 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll try. Any updates on my meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2152-07-29 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve kept your psychiatric meds running. Your ranitidine and nitroglycerin SR are also continuing. We’re watching for any side effects."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2152-07-30 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did well on clear liquids. We’re upgrading to a soft diet today—mashed potatoes, applesauce, things like that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2152-07-30 10:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. I’m hungry. But should I avoid anything specific?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2152-07-30 10:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes—avoid fatty foods, alcohol, and large meals. Stick to small, low-fat portions. We’ll give you written instructions before discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2152-07-30 10:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And what about pain meds when I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2152-07-30 10:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll go home with Dilaudid for breakthrough pain—take it only as needed. Also Reglan for nausea and Ativan if nausea or anxiety flares."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2152-07-31 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been pain-free since yesterday and are tolerating the soft diet well. We’re planning for discharge tomorrow if all goes well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2152-07-31 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great news. Will I need another hospital stay like this again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2152-07-31 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We hope not. The key is managing triggers—avoiding alcohol, eating small low-fat meals, and following up with GI. The EUS might help us decide if there’s a structural issue we can fix."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2152-07-31 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my anxiety? It really spikes during these flares."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2152-07-31 08:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve adjusted your fluoxetine to 20 mg daily—lower dose for now. Continue your clonazepam and imipramine. Talk to your psychiatrist if anxiety remains hard to manage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2152-07-31 08:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I will. Thank you for listening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2152-08-01 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final day in the hospital. You’re still doing well—no pain, eating without issues. We’ll finalize your discharge plan today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2152-08-01 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready to go home. What meds am I taking?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2152-08-01 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll take fluoxetine 20 mg daily, ranitidine 150 mg twice daily, clonazepam 1 mg at bedtime, and imipramine 10 mg daily. Prazosin twice daily, and trazodone as needed for sleep."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2152-08-01 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the nitroglycerin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2152-08-01 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, one 2.5 mg extended-release capsule at bedtime. It’s still being used to help with possible sphincter of Oddi spasm."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2152-08-01 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And Zyrtec at night too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2152-08-01 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, one capsule at bedtime for your seasonal allergies."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2152-08-01 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s a lot, but I think I can manage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2152-08-02 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re cleared for discharge. Your condition is stable—pain-free, eating well, and ambulatory."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2152-08-02 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Any final instructions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2152-08-02 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Continue the soft, low-fat diet and advance slowly. Avoid alcohol completely. Take your meds as prescribed. Watch for worsening pain, fever, or vomiting—return if those happen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2152-08-02 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And follow-up with GI?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2152-08-02 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. GI will call you to schedule the EUS. They’ll evaluate whether you might benefit from further intervention."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2152-08-02 07:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee. I really appreciate all the care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2152-08-02 07:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2152-08-02 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just checking in before you leave—any last questions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2152-08-02 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I think I’ve got everything. The nurse reviewed the meds and diet. I feel ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2152-08-02 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Remember, call your doctor or come back if symptoms return. Take it easy at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2152-08-02 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2152-08-02 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The discharge papers are ready. You’re officially discharged. Transportation is on the way?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2152-08-02 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, my sister’s picking me up. I’m so glad to be going home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2152-08-02 12:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done really well. Keep up the progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2152-08-02 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick call to check in—how are you feeling at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2152-08-02 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. I had some broth and toast, no pain. Resting now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2152-08-02 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s excellent. Keep it slow. Call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2152-08-02 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Dr. Lee? I just wanted to say thanks again. I feel like I finally have a plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2152-08-02 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m glad. You’re on the right track. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2152-08-02 16:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final follow-up call. You’re doing well, and we’re closing the admission. Rest and follow up with GI."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2152-08-02 16:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Thank you for everything."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2152-07-27 23:47:00",
    "admission_end": "2152-08-02 17:24:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of chronic pancreatitis, anxiety, and probable sphincter of Oddi dysfunction was admitted with epigastric pain and nausea following an MRCP with secretin, which triggered an acute flare of pancreatitis. She was managed conservatively with NPO status, IV fluids, Dilaudid for pain, and Reglan for nausea, avoiding Zofran due to allergy. Her lipase levels improved, and she gradually advanced to a soft diet without complications. MRCP findings confirmed chronic pancreatitis and possible sphincter of Oddi dysfunction, prompting GI consultation and plans for outpatient EUS. Her psychiatric medications were continued, with adjustments to fluoxetine. She remained pain-free, ambulatory, and mentally clear, and was discharged home with a low-fat diet plan, pain and nausea medications, and follow-up arranged with gastroenterology.",
    "problems": [
      "Acute pancreatitis",
      "Chronic pancreatitis",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Other specified disorders of biliary tract"
    ]
  }
}
